{# Skills are INDEXED, never inlined, and never filtered. Every page contributes one line: its
   name, the file it lives in, and the `when:` trigger that says who should open it.

   No gating. The trigger does that job -- `lang-c` says "you are writing C", `rocprof` says "you
   are about to profile an AMD device" -- so the prompt does not need to know a task's language to
   decide what to show it. Seven constants used to make that decision, and they existed only
   because an inlined body cost hundreds of lines; a trigger line costs one.

   `when` falls back to `description` so a page that has not authored a trigger still gets a
   usable line rather than a bare name. #}
{% if other_skills %}

## Skills
Each line below names a page under `{{ shared_dir }}/skills/`. READ THE PAGE before acting on its
subject -- the line is the trigger, not the guidance itself. No page is repeated in this prompt.
{% for skill in other_skills %}
- **{{ skill.name }}** ({{ skill.file or skill.name }}.md) -- {{ skill.when or skill.description }}
{% if debug %}# Generated from: {{ skill.path }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
